        "second_opinion": null,
        "why": "Both functions call os.killpg(os.getpgid(self.process.pid), <signal>), but this is only a one-line shared API pattern. close() runs a shutdown escalation: write exit, wait, SIGTERM, wait, SIGKILL, then close the FD, join the reader thread, and clear state. interrupt() sends one SIGINT, resets a command-running flag, and returns a bool. They have different signals, failure handling, and invariants. A helper that wraps the killpg call would be trivial and would not own a meaningful shared contract, so there is no actionable duplication."
      },
